 "not_a_result": true,
 "question": "Is the block offset in the shared cap-response curve predicted by candidate-space size or K completeness, rather than a free block label?",
 "definition": "A_coverage = A / candidate_edges on 12 block-by-cap cells and 72 seed rows. Predictors are log(candidate_edges) and K / candidate_edges. Models are compared by cell and seed leave-one-out error.",
 "method": "Read the committed cap-20/40/80/112 rows. With only three blocks a block-level regression is saturated, so candidate-size and K-completeness models are tested at cell and seed level. Within-larger correlations are reported separately.",
