  ],
  "cells": 12,
  "seed_rows": 72
 },
 "governance": {
  "freeze": false,
  "grant": false,
  "run": false,
  "authorization": "none"
 },
 "reading": "Candidate size can replace the free block offset: its cell LOO RMSE is 0.0184 against 0.0193 for the free offset, and its seed LOO is 0.0667 against 0.0668. K completeness alone is similar at cell level (0.0189) but much worse across seeds (0.0865), and adding it to candidate size does not improve seed LOO (0.0669 vs 0.0667). Within larger-28, K completeness and A coverage correlate only 0.079, while candidate size and A coverage correlate -0.012. Candidate size is the usable offset predictor; K completeness is a correlated regime marker, not an independent predictor.",
